1
00:00:00,734 --> 00:00:03,874
(Hot Debut)

2
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:08,743
(Hyun Moo has something on his face.)

3
00:00:08,744 --> 00:00:09,874
- What's that? - What's that?

4
00:00:09,974 --> 00:00:11,744
- What's he doing? - My gosh.

5
00:00:11,914 --> 00:00:13,443
- It matches the wall too. - What is that?

6
00:00:13,444 --> 00:00:15,053
- Right. - Is he the Tin Man?

7
00:00:15,054 --> 00:00:16,413
- What's wrong with you? - It's about time he ironed out...

8
00:00:16,414 --> 00:00:17,613
- his face. - It was an important day.

9
00:00:17,614 --> 00:00:18,653
So I wore the strongest facial sheet that day.

10
00:00:18,654 --> 00:00:20,724
You look like a sweet potato in my oven.

11
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:22,393
- A sweet potato in your oven. - Gosh, this...

12
00:00:22,394 --> 00:00:23,623
- He's wrapped in tinfoil. - A wrapped sweet potato.

13
00:00:23,624 --> 00:00:24,693
- You didn't waste two seconds... - The inside color matches...

14
00:00:24,694 --> 00:00:25,794
- to mock me. - that of a sweet potato too.

15
00:00:28,794 --> 00:00:30,663
From afar, it looks like you'd be in "Descent of Warriors."

16
00:00:30,664 --> 00:00:32,064
"Descent of Warriors?" That's so funny.

17
00:00:32,264 --> 00:00:34,134
He kind of matches the song, "Descent of Warriors."

18
00:00:35,804 --> 00:00:37,474
- "High-five of the 40s." - The song is playing.

19
00:00:39,504 --> 00:00:40,743
It's so crowded on the street.

20
00:00:40,744 --> 00:00:43,373
People must have thought, "He's doing performance art."

21
00:00:43,374 --> 00:00:45,644
- Like the guy in Paris. - Right.

22
00:00:46,044 --> 00:00:47,543
- They don't move at first, but... - A performance artist.

23
00:00:47,544 --> 00:00:49,013
- they do when you try to film them. - They move then.

24
00:00:49,014 --> 00:00:50,184
Right.

25
00:00:50,414 --> 00:00:52,223
- Come on. Seriously. - They kick their hat to put it on.

26
00:00:52,224 --> 00:00:53,754
(Come on. Stop teasing me.)

27
00:00:54,324 --> 00:00:57,723
(He's quite the spectacle.)

28
00:00:57,724 --> 00:01:00,064
(Glancing around)

29
00:01:01,464 --> 00:01:02,663
- What? - What's going on with him?

30
00:01:02,664 --> 00:01:03,833
(He's just standing still while sneaking glances at people.)

31
00:01:03,834 --> 00:01:05,834
- Yes. Why are you glancing at them? - He's at the most crowded section.

32
00:01:06,734 --> 00:01:09,604
(Is that Kian84 walking toward him from a distance?)

33
00:01:12,844 --> 00:01:13,844
Hyun Moo.

34
00:01:15,444 --> 00:01:17,244
You startled me.

35
00:01:17,984 --> 00:01:18,984
What's that on your face?

36
00:01:19,284 --> 00:01:20,644
- A facial sheet. - What?

37
00:01:21,014 --> 00:01:23,054
I always put on a facial sheet before going to the salon.

38
00:01:24,254 --> 00:01:25,623
- I do that. - You should.

39
00:01:25,624 --> 00:01:27,784
I've never seen anyone wearing that on the street, though.

40
00:01:28,324 --> 00:01:29,353
Does it come with the jacket?

41
00:01:29,354 --> 00:01:31,863
- No. I bought this separately. - It matches your jacket.

42
00:01:31,864 --> 00:01:33,464
Who would wear a matching jacket with the facial sheet?

43
00:01:33,564 --> 00:01:34,963
- Who would do that? - Your jacket matches...

44
00:01:34,964 --> 00:01:36,333
- the facial sheet. - This is good for my face.

45
00:01:36,334 --> 00:01:37,933
I also tried another facial sheet the night before.

46
00:01:37,934 --> 00:01:39,563
It was the one Lingard wore. The PDRN facial sheet.

47
00:01:39,564 --> 00:01:41,063
- Okay. - I wore two of them before bed.

48
00:01:41,064 --> 00:01:42,474
- Good job. - Good job.

49
00:01:43,774 --> 00:01:45,044
Gosh, I'm a bit nervous.

50
00:01:45,244 --> 00:01:46,343
Why are you nervous?

51
00:01:46,344 --> 00:01:48,043
Jang Woo told me you were nervous.

52
00:01:48,044 --> 00:01:49,373
- Being an MC at a wedding... - But...

53
00:01:49,374 --> 00:01:50,713
isn't that hard.

54
00:01:50,714 --> 00:01:52,014
But this is my first time.

55
00:01:52,144 --> 00:01:53,443
No, being an MC at a wedding is nervous.

56
00:01:53,444 --> 00:01:54,784
- It really is. - My goodness.

57
00:01:55,954 --> 00:01:57,654
This is my first time officiating a wedding too.

58
00:01:58,184 --> 00:02:00,824
Jang Woo is finally getting married today.

59
00:02:00,924 --> 00:02:03,654
On his wedding day, Kian84 and I are making a hot debut.

60
00:02:03,824 --> 00:02:06,824
Kian84 will be the MC, and I will be the wedding officiant.

61
00:02:07,324 --> 00:02:08,394
Hyun Moo.

62
00:02:08,494 --> 00:02:09,694
- Na Rae. - That was our trip to Turkiye.

63
00:02:10,264 --> 00:02:12,064
- It feels like a long time ago. - Oh, my.

64
00:02:12,504 --> 00:02:14,433
- I teared up that day. - Jang Woo, the crybaby.

65
00:02:14,434 --> 00:02:15,734
This is my last trip with you.

66
00:02:16,504 --> 00:02:20,643
(The Palm Oil Family's last trip ended in tears.)

67
00:02:20,644 --> 00:02:22,214
- Hey. - Gosh, he's married now.

68
00:02:23,214 --> 00:02:25,044
(Jang Woo stopped crying and said something.)

69
00:02:25,484 --> 00:02:29,154
(He asked Hyun Moo, a bachelor, to officiate his wedding.)

70
00:02:29,484 --> 00:02:31,284
- It was moving. Then I was shocked. - What's going on?

71
00:02:32,284 --> 00:02:35,393
(Kian84 was chosen to be the MC at the wedding.)

72
00:02:35,394 --> 00:02:36,554
(Feeling reassured)

73
00:02:37,194 --> 00:02:41,024
So we need to look better than we've ever looked in our lives.

74
00:02:41,164 --> 00:02:42,934
- Of course. - I invited Kian84...

75
00:02:43,164 --> 00:02:44,294
to my beauty salon.

76
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:46,963
- You went to the professionals. - Jang Woo texted me...

77
00:02:46,964 --> 00:02:48,334
- past midnight. - Right.

78
00:02:48,974 --> 00:02:50,034
Hello.

79
00:02:51,874 --> 00:02:52,943
Your jacket matches the facial sheet.

80
00:02:52,944 --> 00:02:55,014
Oh, this? That wasn't my intention, though.

81
00:02:56,144 --> 00:02:57,573
(Feeling awkward)

82
00:02:57,574 --> 00:02:58,644
You can remove it.

83
00:02:58,984 --> 00:03:00,783
- You're officiating the wedding? - Yes.

84
00:03:00,784 --> 00:03:01,984
- I'm officiating the wedding. - You are?

85
00:03:02,354 --> 00:03:03,583
- Are you the MC then? - Yes.

86
00:03:03,584 --> 00:03:04,923
He's the MC at the wedding.

87
00:03:04,924 --> 00:03:06,254
- There's a hairstyle for MCs. - Make him look neat.

88
00:03:06,484 --> 00:03:08,853
Then could you trim my sideburns...

89
00:03:08,854 --> 00:03:10,754
- and the back hair? - Just trim them a bit?

90
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,563
- And just make my hair look good. - That's good.

91
00:03:12,564 --> 00:03:14,064
Make it look nice and round.

92
00:03:14,164 --> 00:03:15,563
- Give him a neat hairstyle. - My hair tends to spike up.

93
00:03:15,564 --> 00:03:16,664
- Make it round. - Okay.

94
00:03:17,434 --> 00:03:19,664
Just because I'm officiating the wedding,

95
00:03:20,104 --> 00:03:21,603
don't make me look so serious.

96
00:03:21,604 --> 00:03:24,034
Don't make me look old. Make me look young, actually.

97
00:03:25,144 --> 00:03:26,974
Like the wedding officiant for the zoomers.

98
00:03:27,704 --> 00:03:29,444
- Okay. - I want my skin to look bright.

99
00:03:30,114 --> 00:03:31,714
The cotton pads get stuck on your facial hair.

100
00:03:32,184 --> 00:03:34,343
Pieces of them get ripped by my facial hair.

101
00:03:34,344 --> 00:03:35,814
That rarely happens.

102
00:03:37,584 --> 00:03:39,554
(They're getting their makeup done.)

103
00:03:39,854 --> 00:03:42,324
(Hyun Moo is focused on something.)

104
00:03:42,894 --> 00:03:44,594
Gosh, this is crazy. I can't focus at all.

105
00:03:44,824 --> 00:03:46,223
It was my first time officiating a wedding,

106
00:03:46,224 --> 00:03:47,624
so I didn't know the proper length.

107
00:03:48,964 --> 00:03:51,333
You were busy, but you wrote out the speech.

108
00:03:51,334 --> 00:03:52,434
That's dense.

109
00:03:52,664 --> 00:03:55,304
- I wrote 2 whole A4 pages. - My gosh.

110
00:03:55,404 --> 00:03:57,904
(He keeps reading the speech while getting his makeup done.)

111
00:03:59,174 --> 00:04:03,444
(Kian84 is also getting his makeup done.)

112
00:04:04,684 --> 00:04:07,513
(They're dolled up as the wedding officiant and MC.)

113
00:04:07,514 --> 00:04:09,254
- You're good. That's it. - Thank you.

114
00:04:11,824 --> 00:04:13,824
(Someone walks down in a fancy outfit.)

115
00:04:14,084 --> 00:04:16,624
I just decided to wear a suit that made me look young.

116
00:04:16,924 --> 00:04:19,494
It as the perfect example of a dandy look.

117
00:04:19,724 --> 00:04:21,164
(Winking)

118
00:04:22,064 --> 00:04:24,593
(Korea's first unmarried wedding officiant look)

119
00:04:24,594 --> 00:04:26,164
I'm the wedding officiant for the zoomers.

120
00:04:27,534 --> 00:04:28,874
I'm the wedding officiant for the zoomers.

121
00:04:30,274 --> 00:04:31,444
He tried to sound young.

122
00:04:31,944 --> 00:04:34,403
Wait. But you did dress up like a traditional officiant.

123
00:04:34,404 --> 00:04:36,213
- No. I looked young that day. - On the wedding day?

124
00:04:36,214 --> 00:04:37,243
I thought you were trying...

125
00:04:37,244 --> 00:04:38,313
- to look old on purpose. - You looked quite serious.

126
00:04:38,314 --> 00:04:39,983
Why would I try to look old on purpose?

127
00:04:39,984 --> 00:04:41,243
You looked like a character...

128
00:04:41,244 --> 00:04:42,514
- from "The Divine Move." - Right.

129
00:04:42,654 --> 00:04:44,853
You looked like the go player in the movie.

130
00:04:44,854 --> 00:04:47,054
- Really? - You were officiating the wedding.

131
00:04:47,124 --> 00:04:49,223
You would've looked really nice...

132
00:04:49,224 --> 00:04:51,323
- if the suit was a bit tighter. - That would've been better?

133
00:04:51,324 --> 00:04:53,564
Hyun Moo. Even if you did, they would've teased you again.

134
00:04:54,264 --> 00:04:55,563
Why do you keep asking them?

135
00:04:55,564 --> 00:04:57,293
- What do you want me to do? - They would've teased you anyway.

136
00:04:57,294 --> 00:04:58,564
They would've said I was too much.

137
00:04:59,034 --> 00:05:00,664
- We would've said to iron it. - Come on.

138
00:05:01,404 --> 00:05:02,903
I'm the wedding officiant for the zoomers.

139
00:05:02,904 --> 00:05:04,304
(No matter what they say, I'm the officiant for the zoomers.)

140
00:05:07,174 --> 00:05:09,213
(A gentleman is dressed in a sharp suit.)

141
00:05:09,214 --> 00:05:11,684
- This is... - My gosh. Who's this now?

142
00:05:11,984 --> 00:05:13,944
- Kian84 looks great in suits. - My gosh.

143
00:05:14,344 --> 00:05:15,783
My gosh, Kian84. You could go up...

144
00:05:15,784 --> 00:05:17,254
- against Park Jeong Min. - It suits him.

145
00:05:17,684 --> 00:05:18,984
Let's go!

146
00:05:19,224 --> 00:05:20,684
- Don't say that. - My gosh.

147
00:05:20,954 --> 00:05:23,353
- But you did look great that day. - Right.

148
00:05:23,354 --> 00:05:24,393
Your hair and makeup looked great.

149
00:05:24,394 --> 00:05:25,423
He's tall...

150
00:05:25,424 --> 00:05:26,463
- and has a good body proportion. - Right.

151
00:05:26,464 --> 00:05:27,793
- Of course. - With the hair and makeup done,

152
00:05:27,794 --> 00:05:29,233
- he looked normal. - People around me said that too.

153
00:05:29,234 --> 00:05:30,663
- "Normal?" - The ladies said that...

154
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:32,103
you looked so handsome.

155
00:05:32,104 --> 00:05:33,864
- Right. - I heard all of that too.

156
00:05:35,374 --> 00:05:36,734
It felt great hearing that I looked handsome.

157
00:05:38,674 --> 00:05:39,743
It's on me.

158
00:05:39,744 --> 00:05:40,944
- What? - It's on me.

159
00:05:42,474 --> 00:05:44,543
(The wedding officiant pays for their makeovers.)

160
00:05:44,544 --> 00:05:45,814
- Thank you, Hyun Moo. - Sure.

161
00:05:47,044 --> 00:05:48,713
Let me pay for the cab.

162
00:05:48,714 --> 00:05:49,884
I already called one.

163
00:05:51,284 --> 00:05:52,354
My gosh.

164
00:05:53,554 --> 00:05:54,654
- Hello. - Hello.

165
00:05:55,154 --> 00:05:56,654
You're always treating me.

166
00:05:59,664 --> 00:06:01,894
(Writing something down)

167
00:06:02,234 --> 00:06:03,534
What are you writing down?

168
00:06:04,904 --> 00:06:08,173
"Height, 184cm. Weight, 108kg."

169
00:06:08,174 --> 00:06:10,874
- The groom's introduction? - Yes. "Groom Lee Jang Woo, enter."

170
00:06:11,374 --> 00:06:13,304
When he's walking down the aisle,

171
00:06:14,144 --> 00:06:16,613
shouldn't I say something? When he walks down...

172
00:06:16,614 --> 00:06:19,114
I say a few comments when grooms walk down for a reason.

173
00:06:19,214 --> 00:06:21,314
This is their first time too, so they feel awkward.

174
00:06:21,814 --> 00:06:23,954
"Walk down confidently." I say things like that.

175
00:06:24,054 --> 00:06:26,124
"You're the man of the hour." I try to help them relax.

176
00:06:27,254 --> 00:06:28,423
But it's not mandatory or anything.

177
00:06:28,424 --> 00:06:29,424
(Taking notes right away)

178
00:06:29,724 --> 00:06:34,263
And when the wedding aisle is long,

179
00:06:34,264 --> 00:06:35,864
people stop clapping halfway through.

180
00:06:36,334 --> 00:06:37,734
It's hard to keep on clapping.

181
00:06:38,164 --> 00:06:40,734
"Please give a big round of applause and cheer for the groom."

182
00:06:41,134 --> 00:06:42,574
Then they start clapping loudly.

183
00:06:43,434 --> 00:06:44,534
Say things like that.

184
00:06:44,634 --> 00:06:46,544
- Hyun Moo helped you a lot. - Yes.

185
00:06:47,504 --> 00:06:49,214
- "The lady of the hour." - Yes.

186
00:06:49,644 --> 00:06:52,713
But how come the brides get all the attention at the weddings?

187
00:06:52,714 --> 00:06:54,044
Shouldn't grooms be in the center of attention too?

188
00:06:54,884 --> 00:06:56,113
It's the day they look the prettiest.

189
00:06:56,114 --> 00:06:57,314
Don't you know the term, SDM?

190
00:06:57,554 --> 00:06:58,953
They've been taking care of themselves...

191
00:06:58,954 --> 00:07:00,323
- to look the best at weddings. - Right.

192
00:07:00,324 --> 00:07:01,893
It's like a big reveal to the guests.

193
00:07:01,894 --> 00:07:03,624
- People call it SDM? - SDM.

194
00:07:03,754 --> 00:07:05,093
Like the Japanese anime movie?

195
00:07:05,094 --> 00:07:06,393
- "Suzume." - That's...

196
00:07:06,394 --> 00:07:07,664
- That's "Suzume." - "SDM?"

197
00:07:08,234 --> 00:07:09,293
You...

198
00:07:09,294 --> 00:07:10,734
(The movie is called "Suzume.")

199
00:07:11,034 --> 00:07:13,364
Why would you mention the movie? They're completely different.

200
00:07:14,004 --> 00:07:16,034
Hyun Moo. How should I handle this?

201
00:07:16,274 --> 00:07:17,703
"Please give them an even bigger round of applause..."

202
00:07:17,704 --> 00:07:19,143
"than when they walked in."

203
00:07:19,144 --> 00:07:21,814
- "Please bless their future." - Right.

204
00:07:22,074 --> 00:07:23,173
That's such a useful tip.

205
00:07:23,174 --> 00:07:25,144
When the couple kisses, tell them...

206
00:07:25,714 --> 00:07:27,413
they'll start with the family and friends photo.

207
00:07:27,414 --> 00:07:28,483
That's the most important.

208
00:07:28,484 --> 00:07:30,414
There are things you don't need to say.

209
00:07:30,854 --> 00:07:32,184
- Don't say those things. - Don't?

210
00:07:32,284 --> 00:07:33,853
If you're not sure, don't say it.

211
00:07:33,854 --> 00:07:34,924
By the way,

212
00:07:35,324 --> 00:07:37,224
if I get too nervous, could you take over?

213
00:07:38,324 --> 00:07:39,623
I mean it.

214
00:07:39,624 --> 00:07:40,824
(The expert wedding MC everyone can rely on)

215
00:07:41,464 --> 00:07:43,593
I've been an MC at so many weddings since I became an announcer.

216
00:07:43,594 --> 00:07:44,934
- I'm sure Dae Ho can relate. - Yes.

217
00:07:45,334 --> 00:07:46,564
I must've attended 1,000 weddings.

218
00:07:46,634 --> 00:07:48,874
Up until recently, I went to 5 weddings in 1 month as the MC.

219
00:07:49,174 --> 00:07:51,774
When I'm asked to be a wedding MC, I don't get nervous at all.

220
00:07:51,944 --> 00:07:53,703
I just go to the wedding and do my things.

221
00:07:53,704 --> 00:07:54,743
I even do it without a script.

222
00:07:54,744 --> 00:07:56,174
Hyun Moo has done it a lot.

223
00:07:56,314 --> 00:07:57,514
I can do it with my eyes closed.

224
00:07:59,644 --> 00:08:03,154
Hyun Moo, you can write a book on how to be an MC at weddings.

225
00:08:03,314 --> 00:08:04,813
"The Perfect Wedding MC."

226
00:08:04,814 --> 00:08:06,924
("The Perfect Wedding MC")

227
00:08:07,724 --> 00:08:09,093
(Being an MC at weddings? You can totally nail it now.)

228
00:08:09,094 --> 00:08:10,493
(By Writer Jun Hyun Moo)

229
00:08:10,494 --> 00:08:11,524
What is this?

230
00:08:11,964 --> 00:08:13,193
He must've done...

231
00:08:13,194 --> 00:08:14,423
- all kinds of weddings. - Of course.

232
00:08:14,424 --> 00:08:15,863
- You can run an academy. - Outdoors and indoors.

233
00:08:15,864 --> 00:08:18,133
I've been an MC at every kind of wedding.

234
00:08:18,134 --> 00:08:19,234
All kinds of weddings.

235
00:08:19,504 --> 00:08:21,674
It feels so reliable to have you.

236
00:08:23,134 --> 00:08:25,444
(What's the point? He's a newbie officiant today.)

237
00:08:26,374 --> 00:08:27,803
(His lips are dry.)

238
00:08:27,804 --> 00:08:29,443
Gosh, this is driving me crazy.

239
00:08:29,444 --> 00:08:31,684
What tone should I use for my speech?

240
00:08:32,544 --> 00:08:34,013
(Swallowing hard)

241
00:08:34,014 --> 00:08:35,484
He's starting to get nervous now.

242
00:08:36,214 --> 00:08:39,424
(They're getting close to the wedding venue.)

243
00:08:40,584 --> 00:08:43,753
(The closer they get to the venue, the more nervous they become.)

244
00:08:43,754 --> 00:08:45,064
My gosh, this is killing me.

245
00:08:45,994 --> 00:08:47,123
(This is my first time officiating the wedding.)

246
00:08:47,124 --> 00:08:48,293
Oh, no.

247
00:08:48,294 --> 00:08:49,494
(I can do a good job, right?)

248
00:08:50,834 --> 00:08:53,603
"All right. The bride and groom will enter now."

249
00:08:53,604 --> 00:08:54,604
(A few minutes ago, the car was filled with laughter.)

250
00:08:56,174 --> 00:08:57,234
- You were laughing before. - Oh, no.

251
00:08:57,734 --> 00:08:58,973
My gosh. I know how that feels.

252
00:08:58,974 --> 00:09:01,344
But still. Both of them won the Grand Award.

253
00:09:03,644 --> 00:09:05,783
- They come with impressive resumes. - We're both newbies at weddings.

254
00:09:05,784 --> 00:09:06,883
- Right. - Yes.

255
00:09:06,884 --> 00:09:08,044
I hadn't been that nervous in a while.

256
00:09:08,684 --> 00:09:09,754
Oh, no. I'm getting nervous too.

257
00:09:10,584 --> 00:09:12,824
(The newbie officiant is nervous as he's about to debut.)

258
00:09:14,454 --> 00:09:15,524
There are so many people.

259
00:09:16,154 --> 00:09:17,194
Of course.

260
00:09:17,394 --> 00:09:18,863
- Thank you. - Thank you.

261
00:09:18,864 --> 00:09:20,024
(They quickly arrive at the venue before they can brace themselves.)

262
00:09:21,934 --> 00:09:24,394
- You look so handsome. - Hello.

263
00:09:25,164 --> 00:09:26,234
They look so handsome.

264
00:09:28,204 --> 00:09:29,334
Hello.

265
00:09:29,504 --> 00:09:30,504
Which floor is it?

266
00:09:30,505 --> 00:09:31,904
You can go to the second floor.

267
00:09:34,504 --> 00:09:35,974
Gosh, there are so many people.

268
00:09:36,314 --> 00:09:38,044
Oh, my. There are so many people.

269
00:09:40,314 --> 00:09:43,014
(Bustling)

270
00:09:43,884 --> 00:09:46,354
(Welcome to Jang Woo and Hye Won's wedding.)

271
00:09:48,024 --> 00:09:49,954
- That's Hye Won. - They look so good together.

272
00:09:52,164 --> 00:09:54,293
- The wedding hall was stunning too. - Gosh, how grand.

273
00:09:54,294 --> 00:09:55,294
(The wedding hall was as grand as Jang Woo.)

274
00:09:56,294 --> 00:09:58,233
Half of them were actors. The other half were chefs.

275
00:09:58,234 --> 00:10:00,004
All the chefs I saw on TV came to his wedding.

276
00:10:01,504 --> 00:10:03,373
(Surrounded by a large crowd of guests...)

277
00:10:03,374 --> 00:10:04,574
There's Jang Woo!

278
00:10:05,204 --> 00:10:07,643
(the groom, Jang Woo, is taking photos with his parents.)

279
00:10:07,644 --> 00:10:08,944
Look at him. He's nervous.

280
00:10:10,244 --> 00:10:11,373
(His cherished friends have gathered for Jang Woo.)

281
00:10:11,374 --> 00:10:13,844
- They were on our show before. - Oh, it's those guys.

282
00:10:14,914 --> 00:10:16,283
(Ha Jae Suk, Lee Jun Haeng)

283
00:10:16,284 --> 00:10:17,314
Ha Jae Suk.

284
00:10:17,514 --> 00:10:18,823
(Jung Ji Sun, Im Tae Hoon)

285
00:10:18,824 --> 00:10:20,024
- Right. - Self-Made Chef.

286
00:10:20,424 --> 00:10:21,623
(John Park, Yoon Si Yoon)

287
00:10:21,624 --> 00:10:23,423
A lot of actors and actresses came too.

288
00:10:23,424 --> 00:10:25,194
It's like watching a drama.

289
00:10:25,764 --> 00:10:26,824
It's like watching "Jang Bori is Here."

290
00:10:27,294 --> 00:10:28,433
"Jang Bori is Here."

291
00:10:28,434 --> 00:10:29,564
(Laughing)

292
00:10:30,664 --> 00:10:33,104
- Jang Woo. You're so busy. - You must be busy.

293
00:10:33,334 --> 00:10:34,704
- Okay. - I'm the officiant.

294
00:10:34,734 --> 00:10:36,333
(They finally meet the man of the hour today.)

295
00:10:36,334 --> 00:10:38,074
- All right. - You should wear the boutonniere.

296
00:10:38,474 --> 00:10:39,573
- The boutonniere. - Over here.

297
00:10:39,574 --> 00:10:40,674
Wait, wear the boutonniere.

298
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:42,574
Please put it on me.

299
00:10:43,544 --> 00:10:46,484
- I didn't know you had to wear one. - It's for the MC and officiant.

300
00:10:48,714 --> 00:10:51,084
- Look at the camera. One, two. - Hello.

301
00:10:51,584 --> 00:10:52,654
- One, two. - Hello.

302
00:10:53,124 --> 00:10:54,824
Why does Kian84 look so awkward?

303
00:10:54,984 --> 00:10:56,853
There's the facial expression he makes when he's nervous.

304
00:10:56,854 --> 00:10:58,053
Do a cool pose. One, two.

305
00:10:58,054 --> 00:10:59,124
Let's go.

306
00:10:59,794 --> 00:11:01,094
- Okay. Thank you. - Thank you.

307
00:11:01,194 --> 00:11:02,834
- We'll go and get ready. - Yes.

308
00:11:03,464 --> 00:11:05,163
- You're the MC at this wedding. - Yes, Hyun Moo.

309
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:07,163
(The wedding MC and officiant finally enter the wedding hall.)

310
00:11:07,164 --> 00:11:08,434
- Hello. - Hello.

311
00:11:10,034 --> 00:11:11,134
This is the podium for the MC.

312
00:11:11,274 --> 00:11:12,704
Where's the podium for the officiant?

313
00:11:13,404 --> 00:11:14,943
- Is there a table for me? - Yes, there is.

314
00:11:14,944 --> 00:11:16,373
(Where's my table?)

315
00:11:16,374 --> 00:11:17,414
He's going in.

316
00:11:17,844 --> 00:11:18,884
It's just getting started now.

317
00:11:19,684 --> 00:11:21,083
You put it here?

318
00:11:21,084 --> 00:11:22,414
(A cute and cozy table for Moomoo)

319
00:11:24,884 --> 00:11:27,984
(It's in a small corner of this spacious wedding hall.)

320
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:30,054
It looks like a tarot card reading stall.

321
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:32,923
You look like an adult straight up sitting in that corner.

322
00:11:32,924 --> 00:11:34,793
- Oh, my. Goodness. - Yes.

323
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:35,794
I see.

324
00:11:36,794 --> 00:11:38,864
Gosh, I can't believe I'm doing this.

325
00:11:39,734 --> 00:11:40,804
I see.

326
00:11:41,164 --> 00:11:42,433
(The officiant's signature will certify their marriage.)

327
00:11:42,434 --> 00:11:44,334
If I don't sign this, the wedding will be invalid, right?

328
00:11:45,574 --> 00:11:46,943
(Jang Woo needs to get married.)

329
00:11:46,944 --> 00:11:48,004
Okay.

330
00:11:49,114 --> 00:11:51,543
He's the witness to their marriage.

331
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,344
- I'll put it on the podium. - Okay.

332
00:11:58,384 --> 00:12:00,384
This is driving me crazy. Now that I'm here,

333
00:12:00,624 --> 00:12:03,193
I'm getting nervous. My gosh.

334
00:12:03,194 --> 00:12:04,423
My back was getting sweaty.

335
00:12:04,424 --> 00:12:06,464
(He nervously reviews his speech.)

336
00:12:07,464 --> 00:12:10,234
(Locked away in his solitary corner,)

337
00:12:10,634 --> 00:12:13,364
(he focuses on reviewing the speech.)

338
00:12:14,864 --> 00:12:16,274
(Grabbing)

339
00:12:17,304 --> 00:12:19,303
(Downing a sip)

340
00:12:19,304 --> 00:12:20,944
(Downing two sips)

341
00:12:22,244 --> 00:12:23,273
He drank up the whole glass.

342
00:12:23,274 --> 00:12:25,344
Then you'll want to go to the restroom.

343
00:12:26,614 --> 00:12:28,213
I suddenly want to pee.

344
00:12:28,214 --> 00:12:29,314
- Gosh. - See?

345
00:12:29,554 --> 00:12:31,054
I guess I was nervous.

346
00:12:31,924 --> 00:12:34,654
It's been a while since I saw you get this nervous.

347
00:12:36,654 --> 00:12:39,323
(This guy can't stop drinking water either.)

348
00:12:39,324 --> 00:12:41,124
- We did drink a lot of water. - Yes.

349
00:12:43,734 --> 00:12:45,234
(Let me see.)

350
00:12:45,664 --> 00:12:48,574
(MC84 keeps on reviewing the program nonstop.)

351
00:12:52,544 --> 00:12:53,544
What is it?

352
00:12:54,374 --> 00:12:55,743
"The groom will enter now."

353
00:12:55,744 --> 00:12:58,013
My gosh. I'd be scared at that moment too.

354
00:12:58,014 --> 00:12:59,443
When you do anything for the first time,

355
00:12:59,444 --> 00:13:00,884
- you get nervous. - When I was next to him...

356
00:13:00,944 --> 00:13:02,213
It's nerve-racking because it affects his life.

357
00:13:02,214 --> 00:13:03,253
- Right. - Yes.

358
00:13:03,254 --> 00:13:06,583
And the parents of the bride and groom...

359
00:13:06,584 --> 00:13:08,083
only rely on us.

360
00:13:08,084 --> 00:13:09,193
- Right. - That's true.

361
00:13:09,194 --> 00:13:10,453
- No one can help us. - Right.

362
00:13:10,454 --> 00:13:12,423
And there's so much you have to check as the MC.

363
00:13:12,424 --> 00:13:13,963
I thought it wasn't a big job.

364
00:13:13,964 --> 00:13:15,233
But MCs have to check the lighting too.

365
00:13:15,234 --> 00:13:16,333
- Of course. - There are many things...

366
00:13:16,334 --> 00:13:17,393
- they must check the timing for. - Right.

367
00:13:17,394 --> 00:13:19,033
Do you know when the most nerve-racking moment is?

368
00:13:19,034 --> 00:13:21,634
Five or ten minutes before the ceremony,

369
00:13:21,704 --> 00:13:23,173
they make announcements.

370
00:13:23,174 --> 00:13:24,603
- I start to get nervous then. - "Dear guests."

371
00:13:24,604 --> 00:13:26,343
- "Soon, we will begin..." - Yes.

372
00:13:26,344 --> 00:13:27,604
- That makes me nervous. - That announcement?

373
00:13:28,504 --> 00:13:31,474
(Will I be able to do a good job?)

374
00:13:32,944 --> 00:13:35,383
(Turning around)

375
00:13:35,384 --> 00:13:36,784
(Sinking his head)

376
00:13:37,684 --> 00:13:39,623
(Dear Buddha...)

377
00:13:39,624 --> 00:13:41,124
I prayed to Buddha.

378
00:13:41,554 --> 00:13:42,854
So I wouldn't make mistakes.

379
00:13:45,094 --> 00:13:47,193
- This is a piece of cake. - Okay, Hyun Moo.

380
00:13:47,194 --> 00:13:48,524
- Let's do this. - Okay.

381
00:13:48,594 --> 00:13:52,004
And if there's something wrong, give me a signal.

382
00:13:52,464 --> 00:13:53,964
- Or call my name. - Hyun Moo.

383
00:13:54,764 --> 00:13:55,904
Great.

384
00:13:56,004 --> 00:13:57,203
- I'm glad that... - Seriously.

385
00:13:57,204 --> 00:13:58,403
you guys had each other.

386
00:13:58,404 --> 00:14:00,373
Right. You guys relied on each other a lot.

387
00:14:00,374 --> 00:14:01,603
- Of course. - Yes.

388
00:14:01,604 --> 00:14:02,713
In the ten years I've known you guys,

389
00:14:02,714 --> 00:14:03,814
you've never looked closer.

390
00:14:04,144 --> 00:14:05,713
- They look like besties. - Right.

391
00:14:05,714 --> 00:14:07,113
- You always criticized each other. - Yes.

392
00:14:07,114 --> 00:14:09,453
- I got nervous when you went in. - Really?

393
00:14:09,454 --> 00:14:11,784
Having you by my side helped a lot. I relied on you.

394
00:14:12,524 --> 00:14:14,484
(They have bonded over deeply over this nervous moment.)

395
00:14:16,324 --> 00:14:19,264
(Hyun Moo goes back to the solitary corner.)

396
00:14:19,724 --> 00:14:20,793
To the solitary corner.

397
00:14:20,794 --> 00:14:22,664
(Looking cozy)

398
00:14:23,134 --> 00:14:24,793
- Let's go over the script together. - Hello.

399
00:14:24,794 --> 00:14:25,963
- Would you mind? - No.

400
00:14:25,964 --> 00:14:28,804
Please make the announcement at 6pm and 6:05pm...

401
00:14:29,104 --> 00:14:31,103
that the ceremony will start soon.

402
00:14:31,104 --> 00:14:32,603
- In 5 and 10 minutes? - Yes.

403
00:14:32,604 --> 00:14:34,543
I'll stay next to you and remind you.

404
00:14:34,544 --> 00:14:35,614
Okay.

405
00:14:35,714 --> 00:14:37,813
And exactly at 6:10pm,

406
00:14:37,814 --> 00:14:40,243
announce that the wedding will begin.

407
00:14:40,244 --> 00:14:42,453
Then you can start the program.

408
00:14:42,454 --> 00:14:44,483
- Then you can start the program. - Kian84.

409
00:14:44,484 --> 00:14:45,823
Is everything okay?

410
00:14:45,824 --> 00:14:47,384
I'll tell you later.

411
00:14:48,954 --> 00:14:50,054
He wants you to stay in the corner.

412
00:14:51,124 --> 00:14:52,624
"Stay inside, old man."

413
00:14:55,434 --> 00:14:57,093
Gosh, I should help Kian84.

414
00:14:57,094 --> 00:14:58,264
(The old man is worried.)

415
00:14:59,764 --> 00:15:02,804
(Walking up)

416
00:15:03,934 --> 00:15:05,273
- This is your corner? - Yes.

417
00:15:05,274 --> 00:15:06,374
I see. This is your corner.

418
00:15:07,104 --> 00:15:08,714
You don't seem as nervous as before.

419
00:15:09,244 --> 00:15:10,244
No.

420
00:15:11,574 --> 00:15:13,744
You can do this. It's not that hard.

421
00:15:14,314 --> 00:15:16,514
This is nice, right? It's like the Entertainment Awards.

422
00:15:16,684 --> 00:15:17,714
Sure.

423
00:15:18,684 --> 00:15:20,624
(Contrary to what he said, he doesn't look okay.)

424
00:15:21,224 --> 00:15:23,294
- My gosh. - I was spacing out too.

425
00:15:25,094 --> 00:15:27,364
(Are we going to be able to pull this off?)

426
00:15:28,624 --> 00:15:31,094
- There were so many people. - Right.

427
00:15:31,434 --> 00:15:33,803
My gosh. This place is nice.

428
00:15:33,804 --> 00:15:35,374
(A table prepared just for the Rainbow Club members)

429
00:15:35,774 --> 00:15:37,273
You were the first one to arrive.

430
00:15:37,274 --> 00:15:38,744
I was the first one.

431
00:15:40,544 --> 00:15:42,213
(The Rainbow Club members arrive one at a time.)

432
00:15:42,214 --> 00:15:43,843
Check the menu. The meal looks great.

433
00:15:43,844 --> 00:15:44,874
CODE KUNST.

434
00:15:46,284 --> 00:15:47,314
Hey, Kang Yong.

435
00:15:47,444 --> 00:15:48,444
Hello.

436
00:15:49,084 --> 00:15:50,084
Hello.

437
00:15:52,054 --> 00:15:53,453
- Everyone came in order. - Hey.

438
00:15:53,454 --> 00:15:55,124
- Gosh, you're here. - I'm glad to see you. Hey.

439
00:15:55,494 --> 00:15:57,623
It's nice to meet everyone...

440
00:15:57,624 --> 00:15:59,363
after the field day.

441
00:15:59,364 --> 00:16:00,394
Right.

442
00:16:00,594 --> 00:16:01,764
Have you been well?

443
00:16:02,634 --> 00:16:03,863
How are things these days?

444
00:16:03,864 --> 00:16:06,104
I've been working hard at my job.

445
00:16:06,234 --> 00:16:07,364
(Oh, my)

446
00:16:07,804 --> 00:16:08,903
We've all become close.

447
00:16:08,904 --> 00:16:10,474
- Thanks to the field day. - Yes.

448
00:16:11,604 --> 00:16:13,073
By the way, KEY can't make it.

449
00:16:13,074 --> 00:16:15,044
- KEY is overseas for work. - Right.

450
00:16:15,244 --> 00:16:17,214
- I should've been there too. - Right.

451
00:16:17,974 --> 00:16:20,614
You know what? Jang Woo...

452
00:16:20,944 --> 00:16:22,684
He must've been good to people.

453
00:16:22,984 --> 00:16:24,384
Look at the hall. It's packed.

454
00:16:25,754 --> 00:16:28,154
(10 minutes before the ceremony begins)

455
00:16:29,024 --> 00:16:31,054
You can check the microphone if it's working well...

456
00:16:31,154 --> 00:16:34,164
by making the first announcement that the ceremony will begin soon.

457
00:16:34,494 --> 00:16:36,894
- Right. It's starting. - Here it goes. He's going to talk.

458
00:16:38,594 --> 00:16:39,904
- Should I begin? - Yes.

459
00:16:40,064 --> 00:16:41,164
- Gosh. - Great.

460
00:16:41,434 --> 00:16:42,974
All right.

461
00:16:43,234 --> 00:16:44,804
All right.

462
00:16:45,104 --> 00:16:46,744
- All right. - Right.

463
00:16:46,804 --> 00:16:48,303
We will soon begin...

464
00:16:48,304 --> 00:16:49,813
- Right. Kian84... - He's here.

465
00:16:49,814 --> 00:16:51,444
- He's the MC. - He's here.

466
00:16:52,484 --> 00:16:54,213
(Gosh, it's Kian84.)

467
00:16:54,214 --> 00:16:55,954
Groom Lee Jang Woo and Bride Jo Hye Won's...

468
00:16:56,384 --> 00:16:58,254
wedding ceremony.

469
00:16:58,314 --> 00:17:00,254
Dear guests,

470
00:17:01,024 --> 00:17:03,254
please take your seat and sit down.

471
00:17:03,694 --> 00:17:06,063
"Take your seat and sit down?" What's he saying?

472
00:17:06,064 --> 00:17:07,324
He's nervous.

473
00:17:07,964 --> 00:17:09,334
I wanted them to sit properly.

474
00:17:10,094 --> 00:17:13,104
Please put your phone on vibrate.

475
00:17:14,864 --> 00:17:16,334
We'll begin shortly.

476
00:17:17,374 --> 00:17:18,673
- I kept it casual at the end. - Great.

477
00:17:18,674 --> 00:17:20,304
That was great, by the way.

478
00:17:20,474 --> 00:17:23,843
The unique tone of your voice gets people's attention.

479
00:17:23,844 --> 00:17:26,214
- Really? - Yes. It's nice and refreshing.

480
00:17:26,944 --> 00:17:29,184
(He finishes his first announcement in a charming way.)

481
00:17:29,754 --> 00:17:31,884
- You can keep that tone. - Okay.

482
00:17:34,154 --> 00:17:35,353
Great job.

483
00:17:35,354 --> 00:17:36,724
(I just finished my first task.)

484
00:17:37,924 --> 00:17:40,224
(Sighing)

485
00:17:41,464 --> 00:17:43,963
(You can do this, Kian84.)

486
00:17:43,964 --> 00:17:46,163
Wait. Are you the great-great grandpa?

487
00:17:46,164 --> 00:17:48,163
- What is this? - Hold on.

488
00:17:48,164 --> 00:17:49,904
Are you the mountain spirit or what?

489
00:17:50,004 --> 00:17:52,173
He looks like a dethroned king too.

490
00:17:52,174 --> 00:17:53,373
What is this?

491
00:17:53,374 --> 00:17:55,973
He looks like a king who got exiled to a tiny shack.

492
00:17:55,974 --> 00:17:57,244
- Right. - He looks like a greedy king.

493
00:17:57,314 --> 00:17:59,314
That fancy suit looks like the white ramie outfit.

494
00:18:00,644 --> 00:18:03,254
Seriously. It looks like he just lost all of his power.

495
00:18:03,814 --> 00:18:06,583
He looks like someone secretly living at the wedding hall.

496
00:18:06,584 --> 00:18:07,783
A dethroned king.

497
00:18:07,784 --> 00:18:09,324
(The dethroned king, King Moomoo, is secretly living in the hall.)

498
00:18:10,994 --> 00:18:13,164
(The ceremony is about to begin now.)

499
00:18:14,724 --> 00:18:17,533
(The newbie officiant and MC are making final preparations.)

500
00:18:17,534 --> 00:18:19,234
(Utterly nervous)

501
00:18:20,364 --> 00:18:23,874
My expectations are suddenly going up.

502
00:18:25,034 --> 00:18:27,843
(MC84 picks up the microphone with determination.)

503
00:18:27,844 --> 00:18:29,114
Shall we begin? Okay.

504
00:18:30,544 --> 00:18:32,144
(I'm watching you.)

505
00:18:32,414 --> 00:18:34,183
"Who plotted treason?"

506
00:18:34,184 --> 00:18:36,114
"I need to get my throne back."

507
00:18:36,814 --> 00:18:40,024
Dear guests, it's nice to meet you all.

508
00:18:40,254 --> 00:18:41,384
I am...

509
00:18:41,624 --> 00:18:45,453
(Cheering)

510
00:18:45,454 --> 00:18:46,864
He likes that.

511
00:18:47,364 --> 00:18:49,864
