00:29:29,734 --> 00:29:31,674
and the guests at the same time.

774
00:29:31,834 --> 00:29:33,643
I'm quite nervous.

775
00:29:33,644 --> 00:29:36,173
So I hope you will show me support with applause.

776
00:29:36,174 --> 00:29:37,814
- I never knew he got nervous too. - Okay?

777
00:29:37,944 --> 00:29:39,044
- Yes! - Okay.

778
00:29:40,714 --> 00:29:44,184
Actually, singing at weddings makes me most nervous too.

779
00:29:44,284 --> 00:29:46,153
- They only have one wedding. - Right.

780
00:29:46,154 --> 00:29:47,254
- Exactly. - Yes.

781
00:29:47,624 --> 00:29:50,324
When Jang Woo asked me...

782
00:29:50,794 --> 00:29:53,364
to be an officiant at his wedding, not the MC,

783
00:29:53,824 --> 00:29:56,094
honestly, I was quite flustered.

784
00:29:56,334 --> 00:29:57,893
To be blunt, I wondered if he was trying to ruin me.

785
00:29:57,894 --> 00:29:59,164
That crossed my mind too.

786
00:29:59,964 --> 00:30:02,504
The 3 of us met 2 days ago.

787
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:04,174
Here's what he said.

788
00:30:04,904 --> 00:30:08,074
"I want people who are close to me to officiate,"

789
00:30:08,504 --> 00:30:11,314
"act as an MC, and sing at my wedding."

790
00:30:11,374 --> 00:30:14,713
"And I only want to invite people whom I consider special."

791
00:30:14,714 --> 00:30:15,984
That's what he said.

792
00:30:16,384 --> 00:30:18,514
After hearing what he said, I fell for that temptation...

793
00:30:18,654 --> 00:30:20,383
and ended up standing here.

794
00:30:20,384 --> 00:30:21,423
That part was funny.

795
00:30:21,424 --> 00:30:24,593
Please remember that you're a very meaningful guest...

796
00:30:24,594 --> 00:30:28,364
to Lee Jang Woo and Jo Hye Won.

797
00:30:29,494 --> 00:30:32,634
I felt so lost while preparing to officiate the wedding...

798
00:30:33,234 --> 00:30:36,474
that I went to a large bookstore two months ago...

799
00:30:37,734 --> 00:30:40,244
and bought a book titled "A Monk's Wedding Speech."

800
00:30:40,444 --> 00:30:41,674
I read the entire book.

801
00:30:42,604 --> 00:30:44,673
I made preparations to share good words...

802
00:30:44,674 --> 00:30:47,384
and prevent myself from doing a disservice to the wedding.

803
00:30:47,744 --> 00:30:50,214
Although this book is about the wedding speech,

804
00:30:50,354 --> 00:30:53,054
it begins with, "A married couple..."

805
00:30:53,754 --> 00:30:55,654
"must never rely on..."

806
00:30:56,024 --> 00:30:58,354
"or depend on each other."

807
00:30:59,024 --> 00:31:00,824
Isn't it ironic?

808
00:31:01,464 --> 00:31:03,293
Your loved one is often called...

809
00:31:03,294 --> 00:31:05,134
- your other half. - Your other half.

810
00:31:05,494 --> 00:31:08,104
But Monk Pomnyun says this.

811
00:31:09,034 --> 00:31:12,734
"It may appear that two half hearts have made a full heart."

812
00:31:13,404 --> 00:31:15,604
"But that heart is cracked."

813
00:31:16,744 --> 00:31:18,074
"Your spouse isn't your other half."

814
00:31:18,214 --> 00:31:21,244
"When your whole and the other's whole meet..."

815
00:31:21,444 --> 00:31:24,884
"and make a full heart,"

816
00:31:24,984 --> 00:31:27,224
"it's true love."

817
00:31:27,884 --> 00:31:29,853
- He has a way with words. - He really does.

818
00:31:29,854 --> 00:31:30,954
He's the best.

819
00:31:31,754 --> 00:31:34,694
While talking to the two of them,

820
00:31:35,124 --> 00:31:37,264
I filled two pieces of A4 paper.

821
00:31:37,834 --> 00:31:40,264
That was how touched I was.

822
00:31:40,604 --> 00:31:42,563
As I say this,

823
00:31:42,564 --> 00:31:45,874
I'll relay a short message to the two of them.

824
00:31:47,644 --> 00:31:49,073
He hasn't gotten to the point yet, right?

825
00:31:49,074 --> 00:31:51,174
I think that's the introduction.

826
00:31:52,874 --> 00:31:54,114
I think they're beginning to get bored.

827
00:31:54,444 --> 00:31:56,683
There's always someone who can't stay focused.

828
00:31:56,684 --> 00:31:59,823
We aren't used to the officiant's message.

829
00:31:59,824 --> 00:32:01,683
Also, most officiants keep the message short these days.

830
00:32:01,684 --> 00:32:03,553
"Here comes the officiant's message."

831
00:32:03,554 --> 00:32:04,693
"Live well. The end."

832
00:32:04,694 --> 00:32:06,663
- It goes like that. - That's right.

833
00:32:06,664 --> 00:32:07,793
I've just begun.

834
00:32:07,794 --> 00:32:09,563
(Moomoo's message has just begun.)

835
00:32:09,564 --> 00:32:12,434
Although they haven't read the book,

836
00:32:12,894 --> 00:32:15,964
they follow the teachings of Monk Pomnyun.

837
00:32:16,574 --> 00:32:18,173
They don't expect anything from each other...

838
00:32:18,174 --> 00:32:19,374
or rely on each other.

839
00:32:19,904 --> 00:32:21,473
They live their separate lives to the fullest.

840
00:32:21,474 --> 00:32:23,173
They don't ask anything of each other.

841
00:32:23,174 --> 00:32:24,344
They live their lives that way.

842
00:32:25,314 --> 00:32:26,914
He's repeating himself.

843
00:32:27,784 --> 00:32:28,914
(Laughing)

844
00:32:29,444 --> 00:32:31,454
What am I going to do? I'm losing my focus.

845
00:32:33,254 --> 00:32:35,523
It's a challenge for Hyun Moo too. The officiant's message is boring.

846
00:32:35,524 --> 00:32:36,593
(Joking)

847
00:32:36,594 --> 00:32:37,994
When did I say that?

848
00:32:40,094 --> 00:32:41,823
That table is the most distracted.

849
00:32:41,824 --> 00:32:42,964
It's very boring.

850
00:32:43,634 --> 00:32:45,034
Gochujang grilled sole sounds delicious.

851
00:32:45,194 --> 00:32:46,333
Gochujang grilled sole.

852
00:32:46,334 --> 00:32:47,763
- Is this the menu? - Yes.

853
00:32:47,764 --> 00:32:48,834
(They read the wedding menu that's more interesting.)

854
00:32:50,074 --> 00:32:52,573
Lastly, I'll tell you this.

855
00:32:52,574 --> 00:32:54,104
- The last part. - The last part.

856
00:32:54,304 --> 00:32:55,573
It must be the first in Korea.

857
00:32:55,574 --> 00:32:57,374
Upon meeting the two of them,

858
00:32:58,844 --> 00:33:00,914
I've established my belief on marriage.

859
00:33:01,244 --> 00:33:03,554
And I've learned about my ideal type.

860
00:33:04,254 --> 00:33:06,283
Before that,

861
00:33:06,284 --> 00:33:08,884
- I'll also become whole. - I thought that was the last part.

862
00:33:09,024 --> 00:33:11,123
Also, it must be the first since the establishment of Korea.

863
00:33:11,124 --> 00:33:12,194
Kian84 is bored.

864
00:33:12,924 --> 00:33:15,063
Weddings in the early 2000s were like this.

865
00:33:15,064 --> 00:33:16,793
I was reminded of the past.

866
00:33:16,794 --> 00:33:18,033
