01:23:43,268 --> 01:23:45,868
- When it comes to drumming. - Right. Completely different.

2068
01:23:45,998 --> 01:23:48,138
I won't be able to sing jazz even when I get asked to.

2069
01:23:48,608 --> 01:23:50,138
It's a completely different world.

2070
01:23:50,338 --> 01:23:51,338
(I see.)

2071
01:23:52,108 --> 01:23:54,878
(Shall we begin?)

2072
01:23:55,848 --> 01:23:58,818
(The intro sounds extraordinary.)

2073
01:24:00,318 --> 01:24:03,418
(Impressed)

2074
01:24:03,558 --> 01:24:05,818
(Tapping)

2075
01:24:06,218 --> 01:24:07,287
(The performance begins with the lead of the drums.)

2076
01:24:07,288 --> 01:24:08,958
That's so nice!

2077
01:24:09,598 --> 01:24:11,427
- Gosh, that's nice. - Gosh, that's nice.

2078
01:24:11,428 --> 01:24:12,827
(Dowoon's friends perform skillfully.)

2079
01:24:12,828 --> 01:24:13,898
Gosh!

2080
01:24:14,968 --> 01:24:16,838
It feels different with the guitar.

2081
01:24:17,898 --> 01:24:21,638
(They improvise as they perform.)

2082
01:24:22,938 --> 01:24:24,878
(Passionate)

2083
01:24:25,238 --> 01:24:28,408
(The performance builds up.)

2084
01:24:28,778 --> 01:24:31,018
(Controlling the volume)

2085
01:24:31,378 --> 01:24:33,748
(Keeping the rhythm)

2086
01:24:34,218 --> 01:24:35,517
(Jung Sol's bongo solo)

2087
01:24:35,518 --> 01:24:36,588
Oh, Jung Sol!

2088
01:24:38,158 --> 01:24:40,888
(Entranced)

2089
01:24:43,398 --> 01:24:45,998
(Screaming)

2090
01:24:48,368 --> 01:24:50,098
I thought this to myself as I watched them perform.

2091
01:24:50,398 --> 01:24:52,198
They seemed like clumsy guys all the time,

2092
01:24:52,538 --> 01:24:53,908
but they felt impressive.

2093
01:24:54,008 --> 01:24:58,038
DAY6 is about showing our teamwork on stage.

2094
01:24:58,508 --> 01:25:00,907
But this is a place of improvised performances...

2095
01:25:00,908 --> 01:25:04,747
and languages and skills of various instruments.

2096
01:25:04,748 --> 01:25:06,418
There was a different charm about the performance.

2097
01:25:06,518 --> 01:25:08,047
You must have learned a lot.

2098
01:25:08,048 --> 01:25:09,088
I did.

2099
01:25:10,718 --> 01:25:13,058
(Making eye contact)

2100
01:25:13,388 --> 01:25:15,158
(They start playing together again!)

2101
01:25:18,128 --> 01:25:19,528
- What's this? - It's a shout-out.

2102
01:25:19,828 --> 01:25:22,167
"He just did a solo. Isn't he amazing?"

2103
01:25:22,168 --> 01:25:23,438
So this is a shout-out.

2104
01:25:23,738 --> 01:25:26,368
Can't you perform in a club if you try?

2105
01:25:26,568 --> 01:25:27,907
With just a bit of practice.

2106
01:25:27,908 --> 01:25:29,507
- I'll give it a try. - Right.

2107
01:25:29,508 --> 01:25:31,137
- He can surely do it. - We should all go and watch.

2108
01:25:31,138 --> 01:25:32,478
- Right. - That sounds great.

2109
01:25:32,708 --> 01:25:33,747
Thank you.

2110
01:25:33,748 --> 01:25:36,618
I think it will be fun to perform with them on stage.

2111
01:25:37,248 --> 01:25:41,448
I should come up with a routine to work on the basics.

2112
01:25:41,688 --> 01:25:45,188
I want to be able to get into a bit of jazz as well.

2113
01:25:45,558 --> 01:25:50,228
I was naturally humbled there.

2114
01:25:51,158 --> 01:25:52,428
To me, the drums...

2115
01:25:53,768 --> 01:25:55,697
are my friends who always give me the whip...

2116
01:25:55,698 --> 01:25:57,768
without much reward.

2117
01:25:59,768 --> 01:26:01,007
(The drummer with 10 years of experience...)

2118
01:26:01,008 --> 01:26:02,468
(takes another step of growth while watching a different genre.)

2119
01:26:04,438 --> 01:26:09,247
(There's No End to the Path of Learning)

2120
01:26:09,248 --> 01:26:10,778
